  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l as the optimal encoder pair (0.706–0.725 vs. 0.47–0.54 for alternatives), and weighted fusion as slightly superior to concat. All top-3 results use multiprofile + transformer/avgpool aggregation. However, singleprofile with the best encoders has never been tested. config_043 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, singleprofile, weighted) tests whether removing the multiprofile aggregation complexity (which introduces an additional modeling step) could improve generalization while retaining the proven best encoders and fusion. As the final experiment, this is the highest-value untested combination: it pairs the two clearly superior encoders with the preferred fusion strategy while exploring the one remaining architectural dimension (profile setting) that could plausibly shift performance. If it underperforms, config_031 (0.725) remains the best result."
}

